---
description: Guides how UI Widgets interact with Blocs/Cubits.
globs:
  - "**/pages/**/*.dart"
  - "**/widgets/**/*.dart"
type: AutoAttached
---
Interaction between UI (Pages/Widgets) and Blocs/Cubits:
1.  Use `BlocProvider` to make a Bloc/Cubit instance available down the widget tree. Often placed above the Page level.
2.  Use `BlocBuilder` to rebuild parts of the UI in response to state changes. Rebuild only necessary widgets for performance.
3.  Use `BlocListener` for handling "one-time" actions based on state changes (e.g., showing Snackbars, navigation).
4.  Use `BlocConsumer` when both rebuilding UI and performing actions are needed.
5.  Dispatch Events to Blocs using `context.read<MyBloc>().add(MyEvent())` or `BlocProvider.of<MyBloc>(context).add(MyEvent())`.
6.  Call Cubit methods using `context.read<MyCubit>().myMethod()` or `BlocProvider.of<MyCubit>(context).myMethod()`.
7.  Widgets should remain UI-focused; delegate business logic interaction to the Bloc/Cubit.
8.  Use `MultiBlocProvider` when a screen depends on multiple Blocs.
9.  Consider using `RepositoryProvider` for dependency injection of repositories.
10. Implement proper loading and error states in the UI for all asynchronous operations.
11. Use `BlocSelector` for optimization when you only need a specific part of the state.